meta {
  name: Request Sold Deals Export (CSV)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/data-export/sold_deals/exports
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{dataExportToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "format": "csv",
    "from": "2026-01-01"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // A repeat run is refused as a duplicate of the last run's export, which
  // the 409 hands back: either way, that is the export the folder follows.
  if (res.getStatus() === 202) {
    bru.setVar("dataExportId", res.getBody().export.id);
  } else if (res.getStatus() === 409) {
    bru.setVar("dataExportId", res.getBody().existing.id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 202 Accepted, or 409 EXPORT_DUPLICATE on a repeat run", function () {
    expect([202, 409]).to.include(res.getStatus());
    if (res.getStatus() === 409) {
      expect(res.getBody().code).to.equal("EXPORT_DUPLICATE");
    }
  });

  test("is queued, not downloaded", function () {
    if (res.getStatus() !== 202) return;
    const row = res.getBody().export;
    expect(row.status).to.equal("queued");
    expect(row.canDownload).to.equal(false);
    expect(row.expiresAt).to.equal(null);
  });

  test("is named for the agency, dataset and window", function () {
    const row = res.getBody().export ?? res.getBody().existing;
    expect(row.filename).to.match(/_sold_deals_2026-01-01_all\.csv$/);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /data-export/:dataset/exports — request an export

  - **Module:** `data_export`
  - **Permission:** `data_export:read`
  - **Data scope:** never bypassed. Producer-owned datasets (leads, quote
    recaps, sold deals) honour `own` scope — a producer granted the page gets
    their own rows. Client records (policies, households, contacts) have no
    owner, so `own` collapses to the caller's branch, as on the Clients pages.

  **Nothing is downloaded here.** The request is validated, counted against
  the row cap and queued; a worker job (`data-export/export.requested.v1`)
  writes the file to object storage and emails the requester a link to the
  Data Export page. The file is then fetched from the history with
  **Get Export File URL**, until retention (`DATA_EXPORT_RETENTION_DAYS`,
  default 7) deletes it.

  The requester's data scope is snapshotted on the row now, so the file holds
  what they could see when they asked.

  **One live export per request.** A caller who already has this export
  (same dataset, `format` and filters, the multi-selects in any order)
  `queued`, `processing` or `ready` gets a `409` carrying it instead of a
  second one. A `failed` or `expired` export does not count, and another user
  may ask for the same thing. A unique index enforces it, so two racing
  requests queue one export.

  ## `:dataset`
  `leads` · `quote_recaps` · `sold_deals` · `policies` · `households` · `contacts`

  ## Body (JSON — every field optional)
  | Field | Notes |
  |---|---|
  | `format` | `csv` (default) or `xlsx`. CSV is UTF-8 with a BOM and **no formula escaping** — values stay intact for joins; spreadsheet users should take `xlsx`, whose cells are typed. |
  | `from`, `to` | `YYYY-MM-DD`, inclusive, cut on the agency's timezone. Omitted means open-ended; both omitted means all time. No span cap — the row cap bounds the work. |
  | `dateField` | Which of the dataset's date fields the window applies to (see the dictionary); its default when omitted. |
  | `branchId` | Narrows an **agency-scope** caller to one branch (the scope clamps ignore `X-Branch-Id` at agency scope). Ignored under branch/own scope. |
  | `producerIds` | Array. Narrows within scope; ignored under `own`. |
  | `leadSourceIds` | Array. Leads filter on their own source; sales and quotes are credited through their lead (the deal's own as fallback). `__none__` = no source. |
  | `policyTypes` | Array. Every stored spelling matches, raw SmartSuite codes included. |
  | `status` | Array. Leads, policies and households only; values from the dictionary. |

  A filter the dataset cannot apply is a `400`, never silently ignored.

  ## Response `202`
  `{ "export": <history row> }` with `status: "queued"` — the same shape as a
  **Get History** item. The page polls the history until it is `ready`.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — bad date, `to` before `from`, unknown `dateField`/`format`/`status`,
    a filter the dataset cannot apply, or an unknown dataset.
  - `400` `{ "code": "EXPORT_TOO_LARGE", "rowCount": 123456, "maxRows": 100000, "message": "…" }`
    — over `DATA_EXPORT_MAX_ROWS`. Nothing is queued; the refusal is logged
    as `failed`. Narrow the range.
  - `403` — no `data_export:read`, or the module is disabled.
  - `409` `{ "code": "EXPORT_DUPLICATE", "message": "…", "existing": <history row> }`
    — the caller already has this export. Nothing is queued or logged.
    Download `existing` once it is ready, or wait for it to expire.
}
